*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Pipeline outputs (regenerated on each run)
output/
*.json
# Keep test samples
!tests/samples/**/*.json
# Keep config files
!configs/*.json
# Keep coverage outputs and rule manifest
!docs/*.json
# Keep lab evidence exports. These are captured from a live lab that then gets
# torn down, so they are NOT regenerable — the `*.json` blanket above would
# silently discard the only surviving record of a build that no longer exists.
!docs/evidence/*.json

# Screenshots and images — DENY BY DEFAULT, and the default is the point.
# An image is opaque to every guard in this repo: code review, grep, and the CI
# checks all read text, so a credential baked into pixels passes all of them
# without a warning. This repo is public, and per LESSONS 2026-08-28 GitHub keeps
# `refs/pull/N/head` forever — an image committed once cannot be withdrawn by a
# history rewrite. The cost of this rule is one negation line when you genuinely
# want to publish a picture; the cost of not having it is permanent.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp
*.webp
*.tif
*.tiff
# Redacted evidence only. Nothing goes here until the sensitive regions are
# covered with SOLID fill — blur and pixelation are partially reversible — and
# the redacted file has been reopened and visually confirmed. Keep unredacted
# originals OUTSIDE the repo entirely rather than ignored inside it: an ignored
# file is still one `git add -f` or one pattern change away from being staged.
!docs/evidence/screenshots/*.png
!docs/evidence/screenshots/*.jpg
!docs/evidence/screenshots/*.jpeg
!docs/evidence/screenshots/*.webp

# Local testing artifacts
validation-report.json
test-results.json
coverage-report.json

# Logs
*.log

# Secrets (never commit these)
.env
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# Local session notes — these record live lab state (manager IP, credential
# status, which rules are deployed). This repo is public; keep them local.
Handoff.md
LESSONS.md

# Claude Code session state (worktrees, plans, local settings) — never public
.claude/
